# bb-only: the keyword-spelling probe (docs/clean-room-basic.md section 7). Lines 2000-2126 are "REMX" and
# 3000-3126 "REMXY"; the program finds them in RAM after the REM ZQZQ marker, writes each byte value $80-$FE
# over the X (and $FF over the X, the value over the Y, in the 3000s) and LISTs them, so LIST spells out every
# token, statements and functions. It writes program memory only; every PEEK stays below 32768.
#timeout 900
10 A=0:FOR I=1536 TO 32700
20 IF PEEK(I AND 32767)=90 AND PEEK(I+1 AND 32767)=81 AND PEEK(I+2 AND 32767)=90 AND PEEK(I+3 AND 32767)=81 THEN IF PEEK(I+4 AND 32767)=0 AND PEEK(I+7 AND 32767)=7 AND PEEK(I+8 AND 32767)=208 THEN A=I:I=32700
30 NEXT I
40 IF A=0 THEN PRINT "NOT FOUND":END
50 P=A+5:T=128
60 L=PEEK(P AND 32767)*256+PEEK(P+1 AND 32767):IF L=0 THEN 100
70 N=PEEK(P+2 AND 32767)*256+PEEK(P+3 AND 32767):IF N=3000 THEN T=128
80 IF N<3000 THEN POKE P+5,T ELSE POKE P+5,255:POKE P+6,T
90 T=T+1:P=L:GOTO 60
100 LIST 2000-
1000 END
